<article class="env-remark" id="02VP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02VP">Remark <span data-tag="02VP">35.34.2</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $(V/X, \varphi )$ be a descent datum relative to $X \to S$. We may think of the isomorphism $\varphi $ as an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (X \times _ S X) \times _{\text{pr}_0, X} V \longrightarrow (X \times _ S X) \times _{\text{pr}_1, X} V  \]
</div>
  <p> of schemes over $X \times _ S X$. So loosely speaking one may think of $\varphi $ as a map $\varphi : \text{pr}_0^*V \to \text{pr}_1^*V$<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000780070" id="a0000780070-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. The cocycle condition then says that $\text{pr}_{02}^*\varphi = \text{pr}_{12}^*\varphi \circ \text{pr}_{01}^*\varphi $. In this way it is very similar to the case of a descent datum on quasi-coherent sheaves. </p>
</article>